---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site-config';
import { SITES } from '../../lib/sites';
import { breadcrumbJsonLd, productJsonLd } from '../../lib/seo';

const canonical = `${SITES.main}/products/coconut-shell-charcoal/`;
const jsonLd = [
  breadcrumbJsonLd([
    { name: 'Home', url: `${SITES.main}/` },
    { name: 'Products', url: `${SITES.main}/products/` },
    { name: 'Coconut Shell Charcoal', url: canonical },
  ]),
,
  productJsonLd({
    id: canonical,
    name: 'Coconut Shell Charcoal',
    description: 'Natural coconut shell charcoal for hookah and BBQ — dense, low-ash fuel from carbonized coconut shell.',
    category: 'Charcoal fuel',
    properties: [{ name: 'Raw material', value: 'Coconut shell' }, { name: 'Size', value: '25 / 26 / 27 mm cubes' }, { name: 'Ash', value: '≤ 3.5% (supplier-declared)' }, { name: 'Burning time', value: '~60 min per 25 mm cube (condition-dependent)' }],
  }),
];
---

<BaseLayout
  site={site}
  title="Coconut Shell Charcoal"
  description="Natural coconut shell charcoal for hookah and BBQ — a dense, low-ash fuel sourced from coconut shell. Category overview with standardized specifications."
  canonical={canonical}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { name: 'Products', url: '/products/' },
    { name: 'Coconut Shell Charcoal', url: '/products/coconut-shell-charcoal/' },
  ]}
>
  <div class="page-title-split container">
    <div>
      <h1>Coconut Shell Charcoal</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Natural charcoal made from coconut shells — the core raw material for hookah and BBQ charcoal.
        Valued for density, low ash and long burn time relative to wood-based charcoal.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="page-title-media">
      <img src="/images/product-coconut-shell.webp" alt="Coconut shell charcoal cubes beside raw coconut shell halves — conceptual illustration" width="1600" height="900" loading="lazy" />
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>What It Is</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Coconut shell charcoal is produced by carbonizing coconut shells — the hard, dense husk of
          the coconut fruit — in a low-oxygen environment. The resulting charcoal is compressed into
          cubes or other shapes for use in hookah, shisha and grilling.
        </p>
        <p>
          The raw-material choice matters for buyers: coconut shell is denser than most wood charcoal,
          which generally translates to longer burn time and less ash by mass. These properties are
          what make it the standard choice for hookah charcoal.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>Specifications We Evaluate</h2>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Specification</th><th>What It Tells the Buyer</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Size (cube)</td><td>Cube dimensions — commonly 25mm, 26mm or 27mm — and dimensional tolerance.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Ash content</td><td>Residue left after combustion; lower ash means less cleanup and a cleaner session.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Moisture</td><td>Affects how easily the charcoal lights and how consistently it burns.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Fixed carbon</td><td>Indicates energy density and contributes to burn time.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Volatile matter</td><td>Affects ignition behaviour and smoke during lighting.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Burning time</td><td>How long a piece sustains usable heat under controlled conditions.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Ignition time</td><td>How quickly the charcoal reaches full glow.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="callout-pending">
        <span class="callout-title">Data pending — supplier verification in progress</span>
        <p>
          Specific product entries for coconut shell charcoal — with verified numeric specifications,
          MOQ and manufacturer — are published in the product database once supplier verification
          completes. We do not publish unverified figures.
        </p>
        <p><a href={`${SITES.data}/products/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Product Database →</a></p>
      </div>

      <h2>Specification Context</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          One product record in the database carries declared values for coconut shell
          charcoal — the 25&nbsp;mm natural coconut shell hookah cube. The figures below are
          reproduced for context and are <strong>supplier-declared, not independently verified
          by Charcoal Hub</strong>.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Declared value</th><th>Method cited</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Fixed carbon</td><td>≥ 80%</td><td>ASTM D3172</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Volatile matter</td><td>≤ 12%</td><td>ASTM D3175</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Ash content</td><td>≤ 3.5% (typical 3.0%)</td><td>ASTM D3174</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Moisture</td><td>≤ 5%</td><td>ASTM D3173</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Sulphur</td><td>≤ 0.1%</td><td>ASTM D4239</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Burning time</td><td>~60 min (claims up to 120 min)</td><td>Condition-dependent — no universal standard</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Ignition time</td><td>8–12 min</td><td>Supplier-declared</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="meta-line">
        Source: public supplier listing (bbqoncharcoal.com 25&nbsp;mm product page), captured
        2026-10-07. Supplier-declared — not independently verified by Charcoal Hub.
      </p>

      <h2>Buyer Checklist</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Method and basis.</strong> Ask which method produced each figure (ASTM / ISO / GB) and whether it is reported dry or as-received.</li>
          <li><strong>Batch linkage.</strong> Confirm which batch, sample and date each number describes — a figure without a batch is not enforceable.</li>
          <li><strong>Raw report.</strong> Request the laboratory report itself, not a summary PDF or a marketing datasheet.</li>
          <li><strong>Moisture at origin.</strong> Check moisture at origin and again on arrival — charcoal is hygroscopic and shifts in transit.</li>
          <li><strong>Size and tolerance.</strong> Confirm the nominal size class and its tolerance, and verify with calipers on a sample.</li>
          <li><strong>Feedstock purity.</strong> If odour or smoke matters, confirm single-source coconut shell versus a blend.</li>
          <li><strong>Acceptance clause.</strong> Agree the sampling procedure and the remedy for an out-of-spec arrival before ordering.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2>Verification Status</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          No coconut shell charcoal product has yet been independently verified by Charcoal Hub.
          Published figures are supplier-declared and labelled as such; no figure is presented as
          an established fact. Test reports, when attributable and verified, will be published on
          the <a href={`${SITES.testing}/reports/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">testing sub-site</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>Related</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-3">
        <a class="card" href={`${SITES.data}/products/25mm-natural-coconut-shell-hookah-charcoal/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          <h3>25 mm product record <span class="badge badge-muted">data</span></h3>
          <p>Supplier-declared specification values with their source and status.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href={`${SITES.data}/specifications/ash-content/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          <h3>Specification methodology <span class="badge badge-muted">data</span></h3>
          <p>What ash, moisture and fixed carbon measure and how they are determined.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href={`${SITES.testing}/tests/ash-content/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          <h3>Test methodology <span class="badge badge-muted">testing</span></h3>
          <p>How each parameter is measured under public standards, with limitations.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href={`${SITES.knowledge}/knowledge/how-to-compare-coconut-shell-charcoal/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          <h3>How to compare <span class="badge badge-muted">knowledge</span></h3>
          <p>A buyer guide to reading and comparing supplier spec sheets.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href={`${SITES.knowledge}/knowledge/what-ash-content-means/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          <h3>What ash content means <span class="badge badge-muted">knowledge</span></h3>
          <p>Why low ash matters and how the metric is tested.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href="/request-sample/">
          <h3>Request samples</h3>
          <p>Verify a batch yourself before committing to volume.</p>
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="cta-banner">
        <h2>Need coconut shell charcoal?</h2>
        <p>Request a sample or a quote with your size, quantity and destination port.</p>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/request-sample/">Request Samples →</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/contact/" style="margin-left:0.5rem;">Request a Quote →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
